{"timestamp": "2026-03-13T05:50:27.518695Z", "step": "PAGE_EXTRACT_END", "message": "Page 29 text extracted; next: chunk this page", "memory_rss_mb": 950.99, "memory_percent": 25.16, "document_id": "be42fd07-f97f-4e65-a8fb-2f8b2a7a4738", "page": 29, "text_length": 417, "text_preview": "29 Snooping Cache Coherence n The cores share a bus . n Any signal transmitted on the bus can be  “seen” by all cores connected to the bus. n When core 0 updates the copy of x stored  in its cache it also broadcasts this  information across the bus. n If core 1 is “snooping” the bus, it will see  that x has been updated and it can mark  its copy of x as invalid. Copyright © 2010, Elsevier Inc. All rights Reserved"}
